  "body": "## What was broken\n\nBoth uninstallers targeted \\`free-claude-code\\` — a package name **v5 installs never create** (\\`pyproject\\` publishes \\`my-claude-code\\`). Chain on any current release: \\`uv tool uninstall free-claude-code\\` reports *not installed*, the idempotency branch swallows it as success, then entry-point verification finds the still-published \\`fcc-*\\` aliases and aborts — **uninstall could never complete** (fail-safe: ~/.fcc preserved). The process-guard/removal command lists knew only 7 stale names vs the installer's pyproject-derived 26, and tests codified the staleness.\n\n## The fix\n\n- Target \\`my-claude-code\\`; keep \\`free-claude-code\\` as best-effort **legacy cleanup** for pre-5.14 installs; absence of either is acceptable.\n- Command/process-guard lists carry **all 26 published names (both mcc-/fcc- families)** plus a conservative \\`pythonw\\` image guard for gui-scripts running from the tool env.\n- New **parity contract** (\\`tests/contracts/test_uninstaller_parity.py\\`, 206 lines): both directions against \\`(scripts+gui-scripts)\\`, \\`PACKAGE_NAME == [project].name\\`, ghost-name refusal — the class of drift that shipped this bug now fails CI instead of users.\n- Hermeticity repair surfaced by testing honestly: the widened guard collided with genuinely running processes on the dev machine; harness shadows \\`Get-Process\\` under the failing step (pattern-matched to the existing Remove-Item shadow) with two behavioral tests so the shadow isn't vacuous.\n- Rebrand copy corrected throughout; wipe ordering untouched (processes -> tool -> verify -> ~/.fcc last, every failure preserves ~/.fcc).\n\n## Verification\n\nOffline **real-uv smoke** (zero-dep wheel named my-claude-code, 26 shims, isolated tool dirs): phantom-name uninstall no-ops nonzero, correct-name removes every shim — the exact production mechanism through real uv. \\`/bin/sh\\` fixture rig: happy path, missing-primary/legacy tolerance, stale-entrypoint preserves ~/.fcc — all green. Pytest 32 passed / 11 skipped (POSIX scenarios skip on Windows hosts; rig covers them here). **§66 mutations x7 caught by name**, restores byte-asserted. ruff/format/ty clean. PATCH bump to 5.51.2 included (sequential slot after #184's 5.51.1; re-queued at merge if order flips).\n\n## Residual risks\n\n\\`pythonw\\` matching cannot attribute the image to MCC — a false stop asks you to close tray apps and rerun (conservative by design). The real-wheel smoke proves packaging mechanics, not runtime imports.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
