    "message": "fix(uninstallers): target my-claude-code tool name and full published command set\n\nWHAT WAS BROKEN\nBoth uninstallers ran `uv tool uninstall free-claude-code`, but the wheel has\nbeen named my-claude-code since v5.14. uv reports that as \"tool not\ninstalled\", the idempotency branch swallowed it, and entry-point verification\nthen aborted on the shims the renamed wheel still publishes -- so uninstall\ncould never complete on any v5 install (~/.fcc preserved; fails safe). The\nprocess-guard/verification lists held 7 stale names vs the 26 commands\npyproject publishes, and the old tests codified the staleness.\n\nMECHANISM OF FIX\n- Both scripts attempt `uv tool uninstall my-claude-code` first and keep a\n  free-claude-code attempt as best-effort legacy cleanup (pre-5.14 installs).\n  Absence of either tool is accepted; any other failure still aborts before\n  ~/.fcc is touched.\n- Process-guard and removal-verification lists embed both published families\n  ([project.scripts] + [project.gui-scripts], mirroring\n  Get-LauncherCommands); the Windows guard additionally checks pythonw.exe,\n  which gui-scripts run under instead of a shim named after the command.\n- New tests/contracts/test_uninstaller_parity.py pins BOTH directions\n  (every published command appears in both uninstallers; no unpublished\n  names) plus package-name equality with [project].name, the free-claude-code\n  legacy cleanup target, and the pythonw image list.\n- tests/scripts/test_uninstallers.py rewritten onto pyproject-derived shim\n  fixtures and the dual-package flow. preserve-config-on-failure,\n  requires-uv-before-delete and purge-failure semantics kept exactly. New\n  behavioral guard tests (mcc-desktop launcher alive, pythonw host image)\n  use a hermetic Get-Process shadow so the suite no longer collides with\n  processes genuinely running on developer machines.\n\nVERIFICATION\n- uv run ruff format / ruff check / ty check: clean.\n- Whole-file pytest on both touched test files: 32 passed, 11 skipped\n  (POSIX scenarios skip on Windows hosts).\n- Real /bin/sh offline fixture rig: happy path, primary-absent legacy\n  cleanup, tolerated legacy absence, stale-entrypoint preserves ~/.fcc.\n- Mutation checks, each failing its named test, then restored byte-equal:\n  parity direction 1 (published -> uninstallers), unknown-name rejection,\n  PACKAGE_NAME pin, GuardProcessImages static pin, pythonw behavioral pin,\n  legacy-invocation necessity, missing-tool matcher argument order.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
